# Z.AI Rules

Z.AI (GLM) at **GLM Coding Plan** base URL `https://api.z.ai/api/coding/paas/v4`.

## Model table

|| Cursor alias    | Real model       | Description                                                         ||
|| --------------- | ---------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------- ||
|| `glm-5.3`       | `glm-5.3`        | 1M context flagship; always thinks; reasoning_effort + prompt cache (**prefer**) ||
|| `glm-5.3-flash` | `glm-5.3-flash`  | Budget workhorse; 1M context; always thinks; ~3× cheaper than 5.3 (**prefer**) ||
|| (deprecated)    | `gpt-4.1-turbo` → `glm-5.3` | Backwards compat alias; Cursor ~200k context assumption → use `glm-5.3` ||
|| (deprecated)    | `gpt-4.1` → `glm-5.3-flash` | Backwards compat alias; Cursor ~200k context assumption → use `glm-5.3-flash` ||
|| (compat)        | `gpt-4-turbo` → `glm-5.3` | Cursor sometimes rewrites `gpt-4.1-turbo` → `gpt-4-turbo` ||
|| (legacy)        | `glm-4.7`        | Accepted id; resolves upstream to `glm-5.3-flash`                   ||
|| (internal)      | `glm-4.6v`       | **Vision worker** only — describes images for ALL providers. Not user-selectable; not in `/v1/models`. Runs on the coding-plan endpoint. ||

`glm-4.6v` has **no Cursor alias**. Invoked by `vision.Describer`; usage bills under `zai::glm-4.6v`.

## API key

- Key field: `zaiKeyEncrypted` in `config.AppSettings`
