> only. Peak/off-peak multipliers apply (off-peak = 50%).

## Sanitizer policy

|| Model           | Parameter          | Action                                                                                                                                                             ||
|| --------------- | ------------------ | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ ||
|| `glm-5.3`       | `thinking`         | Always `{type: "enabled"}` — `disabled` is **not supported** and fails upstream                                                                                    ||
|| `glm-5.3`       | `reasoning_effort` | Always sent, `low`\|`high`\|`max`. Normalized via `normalizeZaiEffort()` → `off`/`none`/`minimal`↦`low`, `medium`↦`high`, `xhigh`↦`max`, `high`/`max` pass-through ||
|| `glm-5.3-flash` | `thinking`         | Same as glm-5.3 — always enabled                                                                                                                                   ||
|| `glm-5.3-flash` | `reasoning_effort` | Same as glm-5.3                                                                                                                                                    ||

Apply `PolicyZai` case in `applyThinkingPolicy()` and `stripUnsupportedParams()`.
There is no Z.AI thinking on/off toggle (`ThinkingEnabledCatalog` is empty).

## Reasoning effort normalization (Z.AI-specific)

`glm-5.3` and `glm-5.3-flash` always think — thinking cannot be disabled
upstream, so the minimum effort level is `low`. The gateway normalizes effort
via `normalizeZaiEffort()` to the values the catalog advertises (`low`, `high`,
`max` are ever sent):

|| UI label    | Sent to Z.AI                                         ||
|| ----------- | ---------------------------------------------------- ||
|| Off / None  | `low` (minimum thinking — `disabled` is unsupported) ||
|| Low         | `low`                                                ||
|| Medium      | `high`                                               ||
|| High        | `high`                                               ||
|| XHigh / Max | `max`                                                ||

The `ReasoningEffortCatalog` entries for `glm-5.3` and `glm-5.3-flash` advertise:
`low`, `high`, `max` and default to `low` (cost-conscious).

