## Plan concurrency (hard routing)

Z.AI account concurrency (2026-08): `glm-5.3` = **11**; `glm-5.3-flash` = **50**.
The gateway does **not** enforce a local semaphore or overflow to other providers.

- **Chat**: requests go to the resolved Z.AI model; HTTP 429 →
  `doUpstreamWithRetry()` (3×, 250/500/1000ms backoff).
- **Router downgrades**: cheap-class turns (`simple_lookup`, `code_search`,
  `structured_extraction`, `automation`, `subagent`) rewrite `glm-5.3` →
  `glm-5.3-flash` via `config.SmallModelFor`. Already-on-flash is a no-op.
  Editing / complex reasoning / unknown stay on `glm-5.3`. Both models are 1M
  context. Pin `gpt-4.1` in agent frontmatter as a Cursor hint; the gateway
  does not read those files.
- **Vision**: `glm-5.3-flash` (and its OpenRouter twin) keep `image_url` natively.
  `glm-5.3` still uses `config.VisionModelFor(ProviderZai)` → `glm-4.6v`.
  No local vision concurrency cap — `singleflight` dedupes identical images only.

Upstream concurrency is the limit; no cross-provider overflow.

